// Layer_Ingestion_Processing — Data Ingestion and Processing Layer (layer 2 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Ingestion_Processing".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Ingestion_Processing.png
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-data (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi); tool
//   detail for the layer in row 2 of tab:layanan_industri. Included as
//   fig:layer-ingestion-processing.
// Focus: ingestion pipeline (Kafka Connect + Debezium CDC to Kafka/Strimzi, Karapace
//   schemas, Kafbat UI monitoring) and processing pipeline (Flink stream; Airflow
//   batch scheduling Spark and dbt; bidirectional Trino federated query).
// Icons: product logos from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11):
//   kafka, airflow, spark, dbt, flink, trino; the rest are generic icons.
// Connectors: Karapace stores schemas in an internal Kafka topic (Karapace
//   documentation); producers check compatibility against Karapace; Trino <> storage
//   bidirectional (query request and result).
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right), two subgroups side by side, at most
//   two rows of nodes per group, without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer basis: the group label carries its source category (najafabadi2024analysis),
//   namely data curation (data collector + data preprocessor).
// Implementation check: data-ingestion/ (kafka-connect + Debezium, kafka +
//   Strimzi, karapace, kafka-ui = Kafbat UI) and data-processing/ (flink, airflow,
//   spark, trino; dbt embedded as an Airflow task).

direction right

// Source (boundary)
External Data Source [icon: cloud, color: gray, label: "External Data Source (API, files, databases)"]

// Data Ingestion and Processing Layer
Data Ingestion and Processing Layer [icon: download, color: orange, label: "Data Ingestion and Processing Layer (data curation)"] {
  Ingestion Pipeline [icon: inbox] {
    Kafka Connect [icon: plug, label: "Kafka Connect + Debezium (CDC)"]
    Kafka [icon: kafka, label: "Apache Kafka (Strimzi)"]
    Karapace [icon: file-text, label: "Karapace (schema registry)"]
    Kafbat UI [icon: monitor, label: "Kafbat UI (monitoring)"]
  }
  Processing Pipeline [icon: cog] {
    Flink [icon: flink, label: "Apache Flink (stream)"]
    Airflow [icon: airflow, label: "Apache Airflow (batch orchestration)"]
    Spark [icon: spark, label: "Apache Spark (batch)"]
    dbt [icon: dbt, label: "dbt (SQL transformation, Airflow task)"]
    Trino [icon: trino, label: "Trino (federated query)"]
  }
}

// Where output lands (boundary)
Data Storage Layer [icon: database, color: green, label: "Data Storage Layer (Iceberg, ClickHouse)"]
Feature Service Layer [icon: package, color: green, label: "Feature Service Layer (Valkey, Qdrant)"]

// Ingestion pipeline
External Data Source > Kafka Connect: REST + Debezium CDC
Kafka Connect > Kafka: publish to topic
Kafka Connect > Karapace: schema compatibility check
Karapace > Kafka: store schema in internal topic
Kafka > Kafbat UI: topic and consumer metrics

// Stream pipeline
Kafka > Flink: schema-validated stream
Flink > Feature Service Layer: aggregation and stream features

// Batch pipeline scheduled by Airflow
Airflow > Spark: batch scheduling
Airflow > dbt: scheduled transformation
Spark > Data Storage Layer: write Iceberg table
dbt > Data Storage Layer: ClickHouse gold model

// Federated query (bidirectional request and result)
Trino <> Data Storage Layer: federated Iceberg query
